"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1K2YPGE781S0A3Q0\",\"title\":\"Cocoa Biochar Carboneers — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Cocoa Biochar Carboneers\",\"Carboneers\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"CPC1\",\"Crediting period\",\"01 Nov 2025 to 01 Nov 2030\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"CPC1\",\"approval\":\"Completed 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"05 Jan 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"05 Dec 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://Carboneers.earth\",\"t\":\"Carboneers\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.3\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JEXX4F1D1S0TN3V\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JEXX4F1D1S0TN3V/prj_1K2YPGE781S0A3Q0/pjd_1KFASFDMW1S0M5YB/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JEXX4F1D1S0TN3V/prj_1K2YPGE781S0A3Q0/pjd_1KBQJBJYR1S0PGGN/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nCocoa Biochar Carboneers\\nCarboneers\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\nCPC1\\nCrediting period\\n01 Nov 2025 to 01 Nov 2030\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nSummary\\n\\nIn Ghana, cocoa residues remain unutilized, leading to substantial GHG emissions and facilitating spread of pests and diseases. This project converts cocoa pods and prunings into biochar, thereby preventing significant methane emissions and reducing plant disease incidence associated with uncontrolled decomposition of these residues. Given the absence of infrastructure for centralized feedstock collection, Carboneers Coco Kilns are deployed at the village level. Each kiln is equipped with continuous monitoring systems to ensure optimal pyrolysis conditions.\\n\\nGhana\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2025\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2025\\nSite visit\\nCompleted 03 Jan 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nApproval date\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n05 Jan 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n05 Dec 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"